I have just managed to compile the unix version of NetHack 3.1.3 on a
DEC alpha running OSF1. I have used the SYSV option in the unixconfig.h
(both ULTRIX and BSD options give a lot of errors). Being
inexperienced in unix, I have tried to change as little as possible in
the sourcefiles.

None of the 'make':s report any errors or warnings at any stage, and a
2.7 Mb nethack together with the necessary extra files shows up in the
NETHACKDIR. 

My first problem was that when I started nethack it would exit almost
immediately with the message 'End of input?'. I tracked this problem
to the src/cmd.c file and got reasonably good results when I raised
the NR_OF_EOFS-variable from 20 to 200000000. It seems to me like the
program is reading a lot of non-existing EOF:s.

There are still two errors though: 
1. Sometimes the game ends abruptly and unexpectedly by returning to
the ordinary prompt without any error-message.  
2. The game "skips" questions like 'Call a puce potion?' by writing
them out but not letting me answer them.

Does these errors ring a bell?
I am _not_ an experienced unix hacker, so it is quite possible
(probable?) that I have made an elementary error.

